WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.970
What do you see, Mr. Paris?

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.095
Shoes...

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.663
muddy shoes.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.576
The dog.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:14.273
Good. That's exactly
what you should see.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.361
But that isn't possible.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:30.329
I'm sure it's disorienting
to see yourself

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.660
through another man's eyes.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.165
No, I...

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.935
Tolen!

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.200
Now I understand.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.729
I'd better be on my way.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.139
You don't have to go, Tom.

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.335
He's got no right.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.606
No right?
This is my home!

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:47.840
You come into my home
and steal my wife,

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.246
and I have no right?!

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:51.011
That's not the way it happened.

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.711
This isn't the way it happened!

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.310
The trial's over, Mr. Paris.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.345
There's no point
to further denials.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.822
I know about you, Paris.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:00:59.449
I know you were in prison.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.289
That has nothing to do with...

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.488
We'll see what your Captain
has to say about this.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.963
When I'm finished with you,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.329
you'll never wear
that uniform again!

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:08.493
I can't let you do that.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:11.197
No, Tom! Don't! Stop!

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.727
No. I didn't...

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:16.067
Tom, no!

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.281
Let the record show

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:32.450
that the sentence of the court
has been carried out.

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:34.756
For the rest
of his natural life,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:38.161
once every 14 hours,
Thomas Eugene Paris

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:41.565
will relive the last moments
of his victim's life.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.037
May the fates have
mercy on you, sir.

00:03:47.858 --> 00:03:51.692
If the hydroxyproline level
is elevated this high,

00:03:51.729 --> 00:03:54.129
you'd probably call
for a pancreatic scan.

00:03:54.165 --> 00:03:56.156
That's exactly
what I'd call for.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:57.792
All right, then.

00:03:57.835 --> 00:04:00.167
Let's run through the
osteographic series again.

00:04:00.204 --> 00:04:02.798
Just enter the responses
you're sure about.

00:04:07.612 --> 00:04:10.479
So have you given any
more thought to a name?

00:04:10.514 --> 00:04:12.209
I asked the Captain for one.

00:04:12.249 --> 00:04:14.342
Why don't you
choose one yourself?

00:04:14.385 --> 00:04:16.182
Choose one myself?

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:17.619
Me?

00:04:17.655 --> 00:04:20.351
Well, that just isn't...

00:04:20.391 --> 00:04:22.791
Holograms are programmed, Kes.

00:04:22.827 --> 00:04:24.727
They don't choose
anything for themselves.

00:04:24.762 --> 00:04:26.195
Why not?

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:28.289
Because we're not capable
of choosing.

00:04:28.332 --> 00:04:32.769
Well, you choose
what medical treatment

00:04:32.803 --> 00:04:33.963
to give someone.

00:04:34.071 --> 00:04:35.834
I'm programmed

00:04:35.873 --> 00:04:38.808
with over five million
possible treatments,

00:04:38.843 --> 00:04:41.971
with contingency programs
and adaptive programs,

00:04:42.079 --> 00:04:45.207
but it's all programs
upon programs upon programs.

00:04:45.249 --> 00:04:47.740
There's no independent
decision-making.

00:04:47.785 --> 00:04:49.116
I don't see the difference.

00:04:49.153 --> 00:04:50.177
The difference is...

00:04:50.221 --> 00:04:51.188
I base decisions

00:04:51.222 --> 00:04:53.656
on information stored
inside my brain.

00:04:53.691 --> 00:04:55.090
How is that so different

00:04:55.126 --> 00:04:57.651
from the way you access
your programs?

00:04:57.695 --> 00:04:59.993
Well, if you put it that way...

00:05:00.097 --> 00:05:03.658
Do your programs have
any names in them?

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.168
Certainly.

00:05:05.202 --> 00:05:07.432
I have the names
of Starfleet doctors,

00:05:07.471 --> 00:05:10.463
their patients...

00:05:10.508 --> 00:05:11.566
medical personnel

00:05:11.609 --> 00:05:13.941
in historical
and literary contexts...

00:05:14.045 --> 00:05:16.036
So pick a name.

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.139
Just... pick one?

00:05:18.182 --> 00:05:19.479
Pick a name you like...

00:05:19.517 --> 00:05:21.781
perhaps from someone
who inspires you.

00:05:27.992 --> 00:05:31.553
Doctor... Dr. Galen.

00:05:32.563 --> 00:05:35.191
Dr. Salk. Doctor...

00:05:35.232 --> 00:05:36.790
Those are good.

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:37.960
...Spock.

00:05:38.002 --> 00:05:40.664
Can you see yourself
with any of those names?

00:05:43.007 --> 00:05:44.941
Not exactly.

00:05:44.975 --> 00:05:46.636
Take your time.

00:05:46.677 --> 00:05:50.306
After all, you
will be that name

00:05:50.347 --> 00:05:51.712
for the rest of your life.

00:05:51.749 --> 00:05:55.776
Hmm. I never even considered
that I had a life.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:57.219
Janeway to Sick Bay.

00:05:57.254 --> 00:05:59.620
Activate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:05:59.657 --> 00:06:01.022
I'm already on, Captain.

00:06:01.058 --> 00:06:02.184
What can I do for you?

00:06:02.226 --> 00:06:03.386
We've got an incoming shuttle

00:06:03.427 --> 00:06:04.724
with an injured crewman
on board.

00:06:04.762 --> 00:06:05.922
Any details?

00:06:05.996 --> 00:06:10.763
It's either Ensign Kim
or Lieutenant Paris.

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.826
We haven't been able
to raise them.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.532
Sensors indicate damage
to various subsystems.

00:06:15.573 --> 00:06:18.064
You're sure there's only
one life sign aboard?

00:06:19.176 --> 00:06:20.803
That is confirmed, Captain.

00:06:22.747 --> 00:06:24.544
Transport him to Sick Bay.

00:06:24.582 --> 00:06:25.640
I'll be down there.

00:06:25.683 --> 00:06:26.672
Mr. Tuvok?

00:06:31.489 --> 00:06:33.616
They made me leave without him.

00:06:33.657 --> 00:06:35.090
He's severely dehydrated.

00:06:35.126 --> 00:06:37.321
No sleep.

00:06:37.361 --> 00:06:39.454
Neodextraline solution?

00:06:39.497 --> 00:06:40.862
Prepare an I.V.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:45.894
Can you tell us what happened
to Paris, Mr. Kim?

00:06:45.936 --> 00:06:48.234
They made me leave without him.

00:06:48.272 --> 00:06:53.141
They said he'd committed
a... a murder.

00:06:54.945 --> 00:06:57.106
Do you have any idea
who the victim was?

00:06:57.148 --> 00:07:00.379
An engineering physicist
we were working with.

00:07:00.417 --> 00:07:02.783
His name was Tolen Ren.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.788
The Banean Minister of Science

00:07:04.822 --> 00:07:07.814
introduced us to him
just after we'd arrived.

00:07:07.858 --> 00:07:12.659
So, from the other side
of the galaxy.

00:07:12.696 --> 00:07:15.824
70,000 light-years,
give or take a few.

00:07:15.866 --> 00:07:18.664
That's a long trip home
with a damaged collimator.

00:07:18.702 --> 00:07:21.500
If anybody on this world can
help you, Professor Ren can.

00:07:21.539 --> 00:07:22.904
He's developed four generations

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:25.067
of navigational arrays
for our ships.

00:07:25.109 --> 00:07:28.909
We have to stay one step ahead
of our neighbors, the Numiri.

00:07:28.946 --> 00:07:31.039
Did you bring your ship's
specifications with you?

00:07:31.081 --> 00:07:32.241
It's all here.

00:07:32.283 --> 00:07:33.773
Splendid.

00:07:33.818 --> 00:07:35.718
Why don't we begin
to look it over

00:07:35.753 --> 00:07:37.152
at my home this evening?

00:07:37.188 --> 00:07:40.419
My wife would be delighted
to have company for supper.

00:07:40.457 --> 00:07:42.618
There was no reason to say no,

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.958
but if we hadn't
gone with him that night,

00:07:45.029 --> 00:07:46.860
none of this would've happened.

00:07:48.766 --> 00:07:51.428
Oh, come on now, Neeka,
stop that racket.

00:07:51.468 --> 00:07:53.095
They're friends!

00:07:53.137 --> 00:07:56.504
That's better. That's better.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:08:00.067
What a good doggie.
What a good doggie.

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:02.635
Oh, dearest?
Are you dressed?

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:03.647
We have guests.

00:08:03.681 --> 00:08:05.012
I should have called.

00:08:05.049 --> 00:08:07.916
I just don't think
of the common courtesies.

00:08:07.952 --> 00:08:09.647
She's really wonderful

00:08:09.687 --> 00:08:12.884
about, uh, tolerating
my dreadful manners.

00:08:12.923 --> 00:08:14.356
So, you've done it to me again.

00:08:14.391 --> 00:08:16.188
Yes, dear.
I apologize.

00:08:16.227 --> 00:08:18.127
Lidell, this is
Ensign Harry Kim

00:08:18.162 --> 00:08:19.652
and Lieutenant Tom Paris.

00:08:19.697 --> 00:08:21.631
They're from the other
side of the galaxy.

00:08:21.665 --> 00:08:23.132
Hello.

00:08:25.135 --> 00:08:27.626
Nice to meet you.

00:08:27.671 --> 00:08:29.104
You might have called.

00:08:29.139 --> 00:08:30.504
You're absolutely right.

00:08:30.541 --> 00:08:32.304
Do you have enough
to feed us all

00:08:32.343 --> 00:08:33.401
or shall we go out?

00:08:33.444 --> 00:08:34.570
No, it's fine.

00:08:34.612 --> 00:08:36.773
I have some leftover
rolk from yesterday.

00:08:36.814 --> 00:08:38.475
I'll just throw it in the stew.

00:08:38.515 --> 00:08:40.847
Wonderful! Gentlemen,
make yourselves at home.

00:08:40.885 --> 00:08:42.318
I'm going to put on my slippers.

00:08:42.353 --> 00:08:43.945
Lidell will take
good care of you.

00:08:45.155 --> 00:08:46.850
Would you like a drink?

00:08:48.025 --> 00:08:49.014
Sure.

00:08:57.001 --> 00:08:58.628
Help yourself.

00:09:05.509 --> 00:09:07.306
What are you looking at?

00:09:07.344 --> 00:09:09.471
Not the same thing
that you're looking at,

00:09:09.513 --> 00:09:10.571
that's for sure.

00:09:15.419 --> 00:09:17.114
What are you looking at?

00:09:24.361 --> 00:09:27.159
If it's spoiled,
Neeka wouldn't eat it.

00:09:31.635 --> 00:09:34.069
Nothing too fancy
or exotic around here.

00:09:34.104 --> 00:09:35.696
We're very simple folks.

00:09:35.739 --> 00:09:37.707
You're very kind to include us
at your supper table.

00:09:37.741 --> 00:09:39.572
We enjoy an occasional guest.

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.510
I think Lidell would prefer us

00:09:41.545 --> 00:09:44.105
to entertain more often
than we do, yes?

00:09:44.148 --> 00:09:47.413
She's, uh, far more social
than I am.

00:09:47.451 --> 00:09:50.648
I'm afraid she gets
a little bored here sometimes.

00:09:50.688 --> 00:09:52.747
I'm so consumed with my work.

00:09:52.790 --> 00:09:55.384
And here we are bringing
more of it home

00:09:55.426 --> 00:09:58.953
to take your husband's attention
away for the evening.

00:09:59.029 --> 00:10:01.623
Whether you were here or not
makes no difference.

00:10:01.665 --> 00:10:03.826
Tolen would work anyway.

00:10:03.867 --> 00:10:04.834
I'm afraid she's right.

00:10:04.868 --> 00:10:07.496
We are at war, after all.

00:10:07.538 --> 00:10:11.167
By the way, how did you
get past the Numiri patrols?

00:10:11.208 --> 00:10:13.904
Lieutenant Paris
is our best pilot.

00:10:15.713 --> 00:10:18.807
Captain Janeway decided not
to take our ship into orbit.

00:10:18.849 --> 00:10:21.716
She wanted to avoid getting
involved in your conflict.

00:10:21.752 --> 00:10:24.983
So we came in on a shuttlecraft
that would avoid

00:10:25.089 --> 00:10:27.080
immediate detection
by the Numiri.

00:10:27.124 --> 00:10:28.682
I hid behind
the limb of the moon

00:10:28.726 --> 00:10:31.092
before I made a break
for your defense perimeter.

00:10:31.128 --> 00:10:32.993
By the time
their sensors picked us up,

00:10:33.063 --> 00:10:34.963
they didn't
have a chance to catch us.

00:10:34.999 --> 00:10:35.829
Well done!

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.895
Finished already?

00:10:41.872 --> 00:10:43.703
The meat doesn't taste right.

00:10:45.843 --> 00:10:47.310
Well...

00:10:47.344 --> 00:10:50.541
we do have a lot of work
to get done.

00:10:50.581 --> 00:10:52.515
Perhaps we should begin.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.688
We went into the other room
and started to work

00:10:58.722 --> 00:11:01.486
on the navigational beam
specifications.

00:11:01.525 --> 00:11:03.356
It was pretty dry stuff...

00:11:03.394 --> 00:11:06.989
you know, rewriting
baseline code algorithms.

00:11:08.499 --> 00:11:10.160
Tom got bored.

00:11:11.201 --> 00:11:13.726
He left us alone for a while.

00:11:13.771 --> 00:11:16.365
I guess he was with Mrs. Ren.

00:11:18.242 --> 00:11:20.676
I know they saw each other
again the next day.

00:11:20.711 --> 00:11:23.646
That was the night
Professor Ren was murdered.

00:11:23.680 --> 00:11:27.741
Did you talk to Lieutenant
Paris after he was detained?

00:11:27.785 --> 00:11:30.015
No, they never let me see him.

00:11:31.221 --> 00:11:35.317
They interrogated me
for almost two days straight.

00:11:35.359 --> 00:11:38.556
They asked me a lot
of questions about the Numiri.

00:11:38.595 --> 00:11:41.325
At first, they must have
thought we were Numiri agents

00:11:41.365 --> 00:11:43.162
or something.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:47.694
Professor Ren was the inventor
of Banean warship technology.

00:11:47.738 --> 00:11:49.205
He's completely exhausted.

00:11:49.239 --> 00:11:51.537
Can some of this wait until
he's had a chance to rest?

00:11:53.744 --> 00:11:55.974
We'll find out about Paris,
Mr. Kim.

00:11:57.314 --> 00:11:59.009
Janeway to Chakotay.

00:11:59.083 --> 00:12:00.015
Go ahead.

00:12:00.084 --> 00:12:02.177
Set a course for the Banean
homeworld, Commander.

00:12:02.219 --> 00:12:03.777
Aye, Captain.

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:21.498
Come in.

00:12:24.073 --> 00:12:25.472
You sent for me, Captain?

00:12:31.681 --> 00:12:35.344
Lieutenant Paris has gotten
himself into trouble.

00:12:35.385 --> 00:12:39.321
I'm taking this ship into orbit
while we try to sort things out.

00:12:39.355 --> 00:12:44.190
Be prepared to be intercepted
by Numiri patrols.

00:12:44.227 --> 00:12:46.991
They always try
to intimidate travelers

00:12:47.096 --> 00:12:48.791
to the Banean planet.

00:12:48.832 --> 00:12:51.858
The stakes are too high to send
a shuttlecraft this time.

00:12:51.901 --> 00:12:52.993
I want to show our flag

00:12:53.102 --> 00:12:54.797
to make it clear
we mean business.

00:12:54.838 --> 00:12:56.169
I understand.

00:12:56.206 --> 00:12:59.198
Based on your experience,

00:12:59.242 --> 00:13:03.508
what can we expect the Numiri
to do to "intimidate" us?

00:13:03.546 --> 00:13:07.846
To be honest, whenever
I saw the Numiri coming,

00:13:07.884 --> 00:13:10.944
I always left before
the intimidation began.

00:13:13.756 --> 00:13:16.122
Before...

00:13:18.161 --> 00:13:22.359
Uh, however, uh, I know
from, uh, knowledgeable sources

00:13:22.398 --> 00:13:24.730
that they have
directed-energy weapons

00:13:24.767 --> 00:13:28.897
comparable to your own...
uh, our own, that is...

00:13:28.938 --> 00:13:31.600
plus regenerative shields
that may even give them

00:13:31.641 --> 00:13:34.269
a certain advantage over us
in a fire fight.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:37.108
Tell me about them, as a people.

00:13:37.146 --> 00:13:40.980
Are they aggressive, technical,
intellectual, emotional?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.950
Anything that might help me
deal with them.

00:13:42.986 --> 00:13:44.578
The Numiri and the Banea

00:13:44.621 --> 00:13:46.816
are quite different
from one another,

00:13:46.856 --> 00:13:49.552
even though they once coexisted
on the same planet.

00:13:49.592 --> 00:13:52.618
That's why I recommended
the Banea to you

00:13:52.662 --> 00:13:53.890
in the first place.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:56.660
The Numiri have
a remarkably covert society.

00:13:56.699 --> 00:13:58.530
Captain to the Bridge.

00:13:58.568 --> 00:13:59.557
On my way.

00:14:02.705 --> 00:14:04.798
We're scanning a Numiri
vessel approaching.

00:14:04.841 --> 00:14:06.934
They're at combat readiness,
Captain.

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:08.602
Shields up.

00:14:08.645 --> 00:14:10.408
On screen.

00:14:12.248 --> 00:14:13.408
Mr. Neelix?

00:14:13.449 --> 00:14:16.441
A standard patrol vessel.

00:14:16.486 --> 00:14:17.748
Curious.

00:14:17.787 --> 00:14:20.312
Why?

00:14:20.356 --> 00:14:22.415
I would have expected them
to send out

00:14:22.458 --> 00:14:25.291
more than one tiny patrol
to meet a ship like this.

00:14:25.328 --> 00:14:27.956
Let's hope it's a positive sign.

00:14:28.031 --> 00:14:29.259
Hail them.

00:14:30.767 --> 00:14:32.234
They're responding.

00:14:32.268 --> 00:14:33.860
Open a channel.

00:14:35.872 --> 00:14:37.965
I am Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:14:38.074 --> 00:14:40.269
of the Federation Starship
Voyager.

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.505
What is your business
in this system?

00:14:42.545 --> 00:14:45.343
One of my crewmen is being held
on the Banean planet.

00:14:45.381 --> 00:14:47.406
We're on our way to investigate.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:49.213
Consider this official notice

00:14:49.252 --> 00:14:51.516
that you are entering
a war zone.

00:14:51.554 --> 00:14:53.488
You do so at your own risk.

00:14:53.523 --> 00:14:55.514
Understood.

00:14:55.558 --> 00:14:59.255
Any attempt to provide
aid or supplies to the Banea

00:14:59.295 --> 00:15:02.560
will be considered an act of war
against the Numiri.

00:15:02.599 --> 00:15:04.157
You have my word that we intend

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.929
to remain neutral
in your conflict.

00:15:05.969 --> 00:15:08.665
Our only interest
is in our own crewman.

00:15:08.705 --> 00:15:10.798
Proceed.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.775
Your activities
will be monitored.

00:15:15.478 --> 00:15:17.673
Very, very curious.

00:15:17.714 --> 00:15:22.708
In Numiri terms, that greeting
was downright friendly.

00:15:26.089 --> 00:15:28.489
Have all security stations
remain at full alert.

00:15:28.524 --> 00:15:31.550
Continue long-range scans for
Numiri patrols around the clock.

00:15:31.594 --> 00:15:32.959
Aye, Captain.

00:15:32.996 --> 00:15:35.123
Take us into orbit.

00:15:45.174 --> 00:15:47.836
Captain, it's unfortunate

00:15:47.877 --> 00:15:49.970
we must meet
under these circumstances.

00:15:50.013 --> 00:15:52.413
My Chief of Security...
Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:15:52.448 --> 00:15:53.915
Please.

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.408
Exactly what are these
circumstances, Minister?

00:15:57.453 --> 00:15:59.284
All we know is
that a member of our crew

00:15:59.322 --> 00:16:00.550
has been accused of murder.

00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:04.287
Oh, I'm afraid he's been
more than just accused.

00:16:04.327 --> 00:16:07.091
He's been convicted and punished
according to our law.

00:16:09.499 --> 00:16:11.933
What form of punishment?

00:16:12.001 --> 00:16:13.832
The perpetrator of a murder

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:17.033
is forced to relive the crime
through his victim's eyes.

00:16:17.073 --> 00:16:18.938
How is this achieved?

00:16:19.042 --> 00:16:20.566
I can have
our Chief Medical Officer

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:22.601
describe the procedure
in detail, if you wish.

00:16:22.645 --> 00:16:24.044
We have the capability

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:26.708
of isolating memory engrams
in the brain.

00:16:26.749 --> 00:16:29.081
We take them
from the final moments of life.

00:16:29.118 --> 00:16:31.643
After they're used in the trial,
they're transplanted

00:16:31.688 --> 00:16:33.155
into the perpetrator's brain.

00:16:34.991 --> 00:16:40.156
These memories... are used
in the trial as evidence?

00:16:41.698 --> 00:16:44.428
An artificial life-form
serves as host to the engrams

00:16:44.467 --> 00:16:46.128
and testifies to their content.

00:16:46.169 --> 00:16:48.967
In this case,
the victim's last memories

00:16:49.072 --> 00:16:52.508
clearly show Mr. Paris
caught in...

00:16:52.542 --> 00:16:55.409
an embarrassing episode
with Mrs. Ren.

00:16:55.445 --> 00:16:57.072
An argument ensues.

00:16:57.113 --> 00:17:01.743
Paris is then seen by the
victim's own eyes killing him.

00:17:01.784 --> 00:17:05.276
The evidence of his guilt
is incontrovertible.

00:17:18.201 --> 00:17:19.498
Captain.

00:17:19.535 --> 00:17:21.093
Are you all right, Tom?

00:17:21.137 --> 00:17:23.128
I've been better.

00:17:23.172 --> 00:17:24.799
May we speak to him alone?

00:17:24.841 --> 00:17:25.899
Of course.

00:17:31.714 --> 00:17:33.545
That rehab colony
back in New Zealand

00:17:33.583 --> 00:17:35.073
doesn't seem so bad right now.

00:17:35.117 --> 00:17:37.483
Lieutenant, did you murder
Professor Ren?

00:17:37.520 --> 00:17:38.714
No.

00:17:38.754 --> 00:17:40.745
But the victim's
own eyes identified...

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:41.950
You don't have to tell me

00:17:41.991 --> 00:17:43.982
what the victim's own
eyes saw, Captain.

00:17:46.596 --> 00:17:51.056
I don't understand it either,
but I did not kill him.

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:53.466
Were you having improper
relations with his wife?

00:17:54.904 --> 00:17:57.429
Their marriage was over.

00:17:57.473 --> 00:18:00.533
She told Ren they were finished
the same day he was killed.

00:18:00.576 --> 00:18:02.510
That does not answer
my question.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:06.740
Nothing happened between us.

00:18:09.185 --> 00:18:10.777
Almost nothing.

00:18:15.458 --> 00:18:17.517
Tom...

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:22.088
it's very important
you tell us everything.

00:18:22.131 --> 00:18:26.067
Harry said you spent
some time with Mrs. Ren

00:18:26.102 --> 00:18:27.933
while he and the Professor
were working.

00:18:29.705 --> 00:18:31.605
I was bored.

00:18:31.641 --> 00:18:34.474
You know how it is when
two science guys get together.

00:18:36.279 --> 00:18:37.746
I came out of the other room,

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:40.510
looked over
and saw her in the atrium.

00:18:41.751 --> 00:18:44.549
Her eyes were
a million kilometers away...

00:18:44.587 --> 00:18:48.148
staring at stars I'd just
flown by the day before.

00:18:49.525 --> 00:18:51.959
Smoking is a bad habit.

00:18:52.061 --> 00:18:53.722
My species gave it up
centuries ago

00:18:53.763 --> 00:18:56.493
when we finally got it into
our heads it was killing us.

00:18:56.532 --> 00:18:59.695
You must be
a very superior species.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:03.402
That's... not what I meant.

00:19:03.439 --> 00:19:05.532
Maybe I kill myself slowly

00:19:05.574 --> 00:19:08.839
because I don't have the courage
to do it quickly.

00:19:11.714 --> 00:19:14.410
Now, why would you go and
say a thing like that?

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:15.917
- Don't.
- What?

00:19:15.985 --> 00:19:17.577
Don't get involved, Lieutenant.

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:18.678
I was just trying to...

00:19:18.721 --> 00:19:20.621
You'll be sorry.

00:19:20.656 --> 00:19:23.819
Look, I was just bored to tears
in the other room,

00:19:23.859 --> 00:19:25.724
and I thought
you might like to talk.

00:19:37.873 --> 00:19:39.864
Why don't you go ahead
and ask me?

00:19:39.909 --> 00:19:42.469
Ask you what?

00:19:42.511 --> 00:19:45.241
What you've been wanting
to ask me all night...

00:19:45.281 --> 00:19:48.409
what they all want to ask me.

00:19:48.451 --> 00:19:53.514
Why I'd marry a man
old enough to be my father.

00:19:53.556 --> 00:19:57.720
I'd be lying if I said
I hadn't been wondering.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:59.227
He was good to me.

00:19:59.261 --> 00:20:03.357
A lot of other men weren't.

00:20:03.399 --> 00:20:05.765
That sounds like
a good enough reason to me.

00:20:07.169 --> 00:20:09.069
He's a good man.

00:20:09.105 --> 00:20:12.472
I would never do anything
to hurt him.

00:20:12.508 --> 00:20:15.477
I guess...

00:20:15.511 --> 00:20:19.106
that makes you a good woman.

00:20:22.885 --> 00:20:26.252
"Good" can get very...

00:20:26.288 --> 00:20:27.880
boring.

00:20:29.492 --> 00:20:30.982
No, Tom! Don't.

00:20:31.027 --> 00:20:32.619
No. I...

00:20:32.661 --> 00:20:34.322
Stop! No!

00:20:34.363 --> 00:20:35.523
What's going on?

00:20:35.564 --> 00:20:37.623
No!
No!

00:20:37.666 --> 00:20:40.260
Apparently, he's entering
another cycle.

00:20:56.952 --> 00:20:58.510
Is this normal?

00:20:58.554 --> 00:21:02.456
We had some problems
integrating the Banean engrams

00:21:02.491 --> 00:21:04.459
into his alien neurology.

00:21:04.493 --> 00:21:07.087
This is the first time
he's lost consciousness

00:21:07.129 --> 00:21:08.153
since the implant.

00:21:08.197 --> 00:21:11.166
I'd like to take him
back with us

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.531
to our medical facility.

00:21:12.568 --> 00:21:15.059
I'm sorry, but I
can't authorize that.

00:21:15.104 --> 00:21:17.766
Perhaps we should consider
her request, Minister.

00:21:17.807 --> 00:21:20.742
We don't want to risk
general synaptic failure.

00:21:20.776 --> 00:21:23.370
Their doctors might be
better suited to stabilize

00:21:23.412 --> 00:21:24.674
his condition.

00:21:24.713 --> 00:21:28.479
All right, but you're not
to leave orbit with him.

00:21:28.517 --> 00:21:31.281
Minister, we don't intend
to leave orbit

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:33.413
until we prove his innocence.

00:21:37.693 --> 00:21:40.127
Away team to Voyager.
Three to beam up.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.003
It's medicine
clearly beyond anything

00:21:57.113 --> 00:21:58.637
we've ever encountered before.

00:21:58.681 --> 00:22:00.512
What bothers me the most

00:22:00.549 --> 00:22:03.313
is the neural pathway damage
it seems to be causing.

00:22:03.352 --> 00:22:04.944
It appears to be progressive.

00:22:05.054 --> 00:22:06.078
Then this punishment

00:22:06.122 --> 00:22:08.556
could actually be causing
serious brain damage.

00:22:08.591 --> 00:22:10.559
How long it might be
before he's seriously affected,

00:22:10.593 --> 00:22:12.527
I really have no idea.

00:22:12.561 --> 00:22:13.960
I would appreciate
receiving a copy

00:22:13.996 --> 00:22:16.055
of your neurological analysis,
Doctor.

00:22:16.098 --> 00:22:17.429
It's extremely technical.

00:22:17.466 --> 00:22:20.196
To the layman, it would be
virtually indecipherable.

00:22:20.236 --> 00:22:23.603
Nevertheless, I will want
to examine it in detail.

00:22:25.407 --> 00:22:27.773
This might be the basis
for an appeal of the sentence,

00:22:27.810 --> 00:22:28.902
don't you think?

00:22:28.944 --> 00:22:30.206
Perhaps.

00:22:30.246 --> 00:22:33.704
However, before the neural
implants were developed,

00:22:33.749 --> 00:22:36.582
the Banean punishment for murder
was lethal injection.

00:22:36.619 --> 00:22:38.314
It is possible
they would view that

00:22:38.354 --> 00:22:40.652
as the only alternative sentence
in this case.

00:22:40.689 --> 00:22:43.317
Will he regain consciousness?

00:22:43.359 --> 00:22:47.625
I believe so,
but each time the cycle repeats,

00:22:47.663 --> 00:22:50.894
I'm afraid his brain will
take another damaging blow.

00:22:52.501 --> 00:22:53.968
When he wakes up,

00:22:54.003 --> 00:22:56.267
I will require
an autonomic response analysis

00:22:56.305 --> 00:22:58.000
while I question him
again, Doctor.

00:22:58.107 --> 00:23:00.166
Do you really think
Tom would lie to us?

00:23:00.209 --> 00:23:01.506
As an investigator,

00:23:01.544 --> 00:23:04.479
I do not have the freedom
to ignore any possibility.

00:23:04.513 --> 00:23:07.482
Mr. Paris
maintains his innocence,

00:23:07.516 --> 00:23:10.883
yet the victim has identified
him from the grave,

00:23:10.920 --> 00:23:12.319
and the victim's wife

00:23:12.354 --> 00:23:14.948
has testified against him
at the trial.

00:23:15.024 --> 00:23:17.720
Someone is obviously lying.

00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:20.854
An ARA will tell us
if it is Mr. Paris.

00:23:20.896 --> 00:23:22.090
I'll have it ready for you.

00:23:22.131 --> 00:23:25.294
In the meantime, Captain,

00:23:25.334 --> 00:23:27.461
I request permission
to return to the surface.

00:23:27.503 --> 00:23:29.368
What do you have in mind,
Tuvok?

00:23:29.405 --> 00:23:31.270
I would like to examine
the murder scene

00:23:31.307 --> 00:23:33.542
and speak with Mrs. Ren.

00:23:40.382 --> 00:23:41.713
Mrs. Ren?

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:42.717
Yes?

00:23:42.751 --> 00:23:45.447
I'm Lieutenant Tuvok
of the Starship Voyager.

00:23:45.487 --> 00:23:47.614
Would you mind if I asked
you a few questions?

00:23:47.656 --> 00:23:49.783
Are you a friend of Tom's?

00:23:49.824 --> 00:23:51.849
I am the Starfleet
Chief of Security

00:23:51.893 --> 00:23:53.861
investigating
his alleged participation

00:23:53.895 --> 00:23:54.862
in your husband's murder.

00:23:55.897 --> 00:23:57.125
Stop it, Neeka.

00:23:57.165 --> 00:23:59.690
She just doesn't like strangers.

00:23:59.734 --> 00:24:01.258
Based on your testimony,

00:24:01.303 --> 00:24:03.794
I assume this is
where the murder occurred.

00:24:03.838 --> 00:24:06.136
Yes, right there.

00:24:06.174 --> 00:24:08.802
I had to have a professional
cleaning crew

00:24:08.843 --> 00:24:11.539
come in to remove
the bloodstain.

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:12.945
You chose to remain in the house

00:24:12.981 --> 00:24:15.279
after an act
of such violence occurred?

00:24:15.317 --> 00:24:18.616
This has been my home
for over ten years, Mr. Tuvok.

00:24:18.653 --> 00:24:21.645
Do you really find that
so hard to believe?

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:23.590
I am a Vulcan, Mrs. Ren.

00:24:23.625 --> 00:24:26.150
By nature, we are
a dispassionate people.

00:24:26.194 --> 00:24:29.857
It is rare to encounter someone
as dispassionate as we are.

00:24:29.898 --> 00:24:32.423
Dispassionate?

00:24:32.467 --> 00:24:35.664
Is that how I seem to you?

00:24:35.704 --> 00:24:40.300
I think you'd get an argument
from Tom Paris.

00:24:43.378 --> 00:24:44.640
Can I get you a drink?

00:24:44.679 --> 00:24:46.977
Thank you, no.

00:24:47.082 --> 00:24:48.572
Mind if I have one?

00:24:48.617 --> 00:24:50.915
Please.

00:24:50.952 --> 00:24:52.681
You testified at the trial

00:24:52.721 --> 00:24:55.121
that you and your husband
had an argument the afternoon

00:24:55.156 --> 00:24:56.521
before he was killed.

00:24:57.959 --> 00:25:00.951
I never said there was
an argument, Lieutenant.

00:25:03.298 --> 00:25:05.823
Have you ever had
to end a marriage?

00:25:05.867 --> 00:25:07.095
No.

00:25:09.237 --> 00:25:11.262
Are you married?

00:25:11.306 --> 00:25:15.174
My wife and I have been married
for 67 years.

00:25:15.210 --> 00:25:18.771
I'm sure she's a fine,
dispassionate woman.

00:25:20.682 --> 00:25:23.617
I hope you never have
to find out for yourself,

00:25:23.652 --> 00:25:27.611
but I can tell you,
ending a marriage...

00:25:27.656 --> 00:25:29.749
it's a quiet thing.

00:25:29.791 --> 00:25:31.782
The arguments are long over

00:25:31.826 --> 00:25:35.557
and there's really nothing much
left to say at all.

00:25:35.597 --> 00:25:38.896
May I ask why you decided
at this time

00:25:38.933 --> 00:25:41.094
to end your marriage
to Professor Ren?

00:25:41.136 --> 00:25:43.696
Because I was attracted
to another man.

00:25:43.738 --> 00:25:47.469
I didn't want to deceive
my husband.

00:25:47.509 --> 00:25:50.478
That other man
was Lieutenant Paris?

00:25:51.946 --> 00:25:53.709
Lieutenant Paris would have been

00:25:53.748 --> 00:25:55.716
departing this planet
in a few days,

00:25:55.750 --> 00:25:59.652
and yet, you left your husband
of ten years for him.

00:25:59.688 --> 00:26:03.124
Meeting Tom
gave me the push I needed.

00:26:03.158 --> 00:26:07.652
I already knew in my heart
that it was time to start over.

00:26:07.696 --> 00:26:09.254
Exactly when did you
see Mr. Paris

00:26:09.297 --> 00:26:10.855
on the day of the murder?

00:26:10.899 --> 00:26:13.459
I went to see him
at the Engineering Institute

00:26:13.501 --> 00:26:15.298
after I talked with my husband.

00:26:15.336 --> 00:26:20.137
Once I was free, I knew
he wanted to be with me.

00:26:20.175 --> 00:26:21.403
How did you know?

00:26:22.877 --> 00:26:25.072
A woman knows, Lieutenant.

00:26:26.114 --> 00:26:27.513
He left his friend Harry

00:26:27.549 --> 00:26:29.449
to finish
the technical research

00:26:29.484 --> 00:26:30.542
and walked me home.

00:26:30.585 --> 00:26:32.712
We were caught in a cloudburst
on the way.

00:26:32.754 --> 00:26:35.951
Oh, I'm completely soaked.

00:26:36.057 --> 00:26:38.582
There must be a centimeter
of water in my boots.

00:26:38.626 --> 00:26:39.923
Here, let me help you.

00:27:07.622 --> 00:27:08.919
We shouldn't.

00:27:08.990 --> 00:27:10.480
It's okay.

00:27:10.525 --> 00:27:12.117
He knows it's over.

00:27:12.160 --> 00:27:14.253
But you're still
a married woman.

00:27:14.295 --> 00:27:18.231
I haven't been married
for years, Tom.

00:27:18.266 --> 00:27:21.463
To him, I'm a friend,
a companion.

00:27:21.503 --> 00:27:25.166
He hasn't treated me
like a woman since...

00:27:25.206 --> 00:27:27.367
It must have been
the day of the eclipse

00:27:27.408 --> 00:27:29.239
four years ago.

00:27:29.277 --> 00:27:30.539
Eclipse?

00:27:30.578 --> 00:27:32.944
He was very excited
by the eclipse.

00:27:32.981 --> 00:27:34.573
Don't ask me why.

00:27:34.616 --> 00:27:37.881
Our timing's just a little off.

00:27:37.919 --> 00:27:40.752
You'll be gone in a few days.

00:27:40.789 --> 00:27:43.553
This is the only time we've got.

00:27:50.932 --> 00:27:54.368
Let me make you something
to warm you up.

00:27:54.402 --> 00:27:58.600
I love to drink Marob root tea
on rainy afternoons.

00:28:02.610 --> 00:28:03.907
I made some tea.

00:28:04.012 --> 00:28:05.843
We talked for a while.

00:28:05.880 --> 00:28:10.681
Then we went out to the atrium
to watch the storm...

00:28:10.718 --> 00:28:12.549
and the rest you know.

00:28:12.587 --> 00:28:15.647
Did you leave the room
at any time during the fight

00:28:15.690 --> 00:28:17.590
between your husband
and Lieutenant Paris?

00:28:19.961 --> 00:28:23.328
I saw Tom murder
my husband, Mr. Tuvok.

00:28:23.364 --> 00:28:26.527
I tried to stop him.
I couldn't.

00:28:26.568 --> 00:28:27.933
Voyager to Tuvok.

00:28:27.969 --> 00:28:29.937
This is Lieutenant Tuvok.

00:28:30.004 --> 00:28:31.562
Mr. Paris has regained
consciousness.

00:28:31.606 --> 00:28:32.868
I thought you'd want to know.

00:28:32.907 --> 00:28:33.874
Thank you.

00:28:33.908 --> 00:28:35.375
I'll be returning shortly.

00:28:35.410 --> 00:28:36.809
Tuvok out.

00:28:36.845 --> 00:28:39.109
Thank you for your help,
Mrs. Ren.

00:28:42.984 --> 00:28:44.918
Lieutenant.

00:28:44.953 --> 00:28:47.615
When you see Tom...

00:28:47.655 --> 00:28:50.522
would you tell him that I...

00:28:50.558 --> 00:28:51.855
forgive him?

00:29:02.136 --> 00:29:05.799
Everything she told you
is true.

00:29:05.840 --> 00:29:08.400
Except I don't remember
going into the atrium

00:29:08.443 --> 00:29:10.070
or anything else after that.

00:29:10.111 --> 00:29:12.511
The last thing you remember is?

00:29:12.547 --> 00:29:15.380
Sitting with her,
drinking tea...

00:29:15.416 --> 00:29:18.442
talking about the sensual
effects of eclipses...

00:29:22.457 --> 00:29:25.358
After that I must have
fallen asleep.

00:29:25.393 --> 00:29:27.418
When I woke up, I was in a cell.

00:29:29.764 --> 00:29:31.789
He's telling you the truth.

00:29:33.501 --> 00:29:35.628
Was there any evidence
of a sedative in his system

00:29:35.670 --> 00:29:36.637
when he returned here?

00:29:36.671 --> 00:29:38.434
The Banean medical
authorities checked him.

00:29:38.473 --> 00:29:40.373
They didn't find
any drugs in his blood.

00:29:40.408 --> 00:29:42.342
Most narcotics would have
been gone from his system

00:29:42.377 --> 00:29:43.401
by the time he got to me.

00:29:45.947 --> 00:29:47.107
Chakotay to Tuvok.

00:29:47.148 --> 00:29:48.945
You're needed on the Bridge.

00:29:49.050 --> 00:29:51.041
We're under attack
by Numiri patrols.

00:29:51.085 --> 00:29:52.587
On my way, Commander.

00:29:59.093 --> 00:30:01.323
Evasive pattern Beta 140.

00:30:01.362 --> 00:30:02.954
Dual attack mode.

00:30:03.064 --> 00:30:05.259
Evasive pattern confirmed.

00:30:05.299 --> 00:30:07.233
They're attempting to lock
a tractor beam on us.

00:30:07.268 --> 00:30:09.259
That is a standard tactic
for the Numiri

00:30:09.303 --> 00:30:10.895
when they intend
to board your vessel.

00:30:10.938 --> 00:30:12.371
Well, at least now you know

00:30:12.406 --> 00:30:14.840
I was telling the truth
about them, Captain.

00:30:17.244 --> 00:30:20.077
Although I take no pleasure
in being right, mind you.

00:30:20.114 --> 00:30:21.138
But why now?

00:30:21.182 --> 00:30:22.513
Why an unprovoked attack?

00:30:22.550 --> 00:30:23.608
What are they after?

00:30:23.651 --> 00:30:26.415
The Numiri have never needed
an excuse to attack anyone.

00:30:28.656 --> 00:30:30.283
Shields at 90 percent
and holding.

00:30:30.324 --> 00:30:35.227
Commander, prepare to initiate
attack maneuver Kappa 010.

00:30:35.262 --> 00:30:36.820
Captain, if you don't mind...

00:30:36.864 --> 00:30:39.094
there's a Maquis trick
we sometimes use

00:30:39.133 --> 00:30:41.328
to get out
of situations like this.

00:30:41.369 --> 00:30:42.859
Be my guest.

00:30:43.871 --> 00:30:45.998
B'Elanna, remember
Teluridian IV?

00:30:46.073 --> 00:30:47.904
The two Starfleet runabouts?

00:30:47.942 --> 00:30:49.000
I'm with you.

00:30:49.110 --> 00:30:50.941
Blowing out
the dorsal phase emitters.

00:30:50.978 --> 00:30:52.002
Torres to Engineering.

00:30:52.113 --> 00:30:53.205
Go ahead.

00:30:53.247 --> 00:30:55.681
Vent a couple
of LN-2 exhaust conduits

00:30:55.716 --> 00:30:57.206
along the dorsal emitters.

00:30:57.251 --> 00:30:58.684
Make it look like
we're in serious trouble.

00:30:58.719 --> 00:31:00.584
Understood.

00:31:00.621 --> 00:31:02.452
Cut all engines.

00:31:02.490 --> 00:31:03.855
Engines off-line.

00:31:03.891 --> 00:31:06.951
Tuvok, lock phasers on
their navigational deflectors.

00:31:07.028 --> 00:31:08.689
Acknowledged.

00:31:08.729 --> 00:31:11.061
Numiri ships are closing.

00:31:11.098 --> 00:31:12.292
4,000 kilometers.

00:31:12.333 --> 00:31:15.928
Not to belittle Maquis tactics,
Commander, but this is

00:31:15.970 --> 00:31:17.267
a very old trick.

00:31:17.304 --> 00:31:19.795
It worked against those
Starfleet runabouts.

00:31:19.840 --> 00:31:21.967
You're lucky I wasn't
commanding one of them.

00:31:22.076 --> 00:31:23.976
2,000 kilometers.

00:31:24.011 --> 00:31:26.343
Besides,
out here in the Delta Quadrant,

00:31:26.380 --> 00:31:27.972
every old trick is new again.

00:31:28.049 --> 00:31:30.210
1,500 kilometers.

00:31:30.251 --> 00:31:32.082
They're sending out
tractor beams again.

00:31:32.119 --> 00:31:33.552
That's our cue.

00:31:34.889 --> 00:31:36.447
Fire phasers.

00:31:36.490 --> 00:31:38.481
Engage impulse engines.

00:31:48.269 --> 00:31:50.362
Both Numiri vessels
are disabled, Captain.

00:31:55.242 --> 00:31:56.573
That's one trick you won't

00:31:56.610 --> 00:31:58.544
be able to use again
when we get back.

00:31:58.579 --> 00:32:00.308
I have more.

00:32:00.347 --> 00:32:01.678
Cancel Red Alert.

00:32:01.716 --> 00:32:03.183
Take us into high orbit.

00:32:03.217 --> 00:32:04.946
Captain.

00:32:05.019 --> 00:32:07.681
More Numiri will be coming.

00:32:07.722 --> 00:32:08.950
I promise you.

00:32:09.023 --> 00:32:13.084
Mr. Tuvok, any progress
with your investigation?

00:32:13.127 --> 00:32:15.721
Based on the ARA, I am convinced

00:32:15.763 --> 00:32:17.560
Lieutenant Paris
believes what he is saying.

00:32:17.598 --> 00:32:21.591
However, I can offer no tangible
evidence on his behalf.

00:32:21.635 --> 00:32:23.967
Considering the urgency
of the situation,

00:32:24.071 --> 00:32:26.505
I believe
the only logical alternative

00:32:26.540 --> 00:32:29.407
at this time
is to witness the crime myself.

00:32:29.443 --> 00:32:31.206
Yourself?

00:32:31.245 --> 00:32:34.271
I propose a mind-meld
with Lieutenant Paris.

00:32:34.315 --> 00:32:35.646
A-a what?

00:32:35.683 --> 00:32:36.650
What, what did he say?

00:32:36.684 --> 00:32:38.515
A mind what?

00:32:42.223 --> 00:32:43.781
Let me tell you something,
Lieutenant.

00:32:43.824 --> 00:32:45.155
Believe it or not,

00:32:45.192 --> 00:32:47.558
I know more about mind-melds
than you do.

00:32:47.595 --> 00:32:49.222
I know what every
Vulcan doctor has said

00:32:49.263 --> 00:32:51.527
in every study of mind-melds,
and I still cannot tell you

00:32:51.565 --> 00:32:53.157
what will happen if you do this.

00:32:53.200 --> 00:32:55.327
If these cycles cause damage
to a human brain,

00:32:55.369 --> 00:32:57.735
there's no telling what the risk
might be to a Vulcan.

00:32:57.772 --> 00:33:00.002
I've examined your neurological
reports, Doctor,

00:33:00.107 --> 00:33:02.132
and I believe the risk
is acceptable.

00:33:02.176 --> 00:33:03.734
- Tuvok...
- Captain...

00:33:03.778 --> 00:33:05.473
the answers I seek
can only be found

00:33:05.513 --> 00:33:07.071
in the eyes of the murdered man.

00:33:07.114 --> 00:33:10.140
It may be our only chance to
prove Lieutenant Paris innocent.

00:33:10.184 --> 00:33:11.981
Tom?

00:33:53.961 --> 00:33:55.087
Tolen!

00:33:55.129 --> 00:33:57.495
Now I understand.

00:33:57.531 --> 00:33:58.896
I'd better be on my way.

00:34:03.204 --> 00:34:04.933
You don't have to go, Tom.

00:34:05.005 --> 00:34:06.097
He's got no right.

00:34:06.140 --> 00:34:07.937
No right?
This is my home!

00:34:08.042 --> 00:34:10.602
You come into my home
and steal my wife,

00:34:10.644 --> 00:34:12.043
and I have no right?!

00:34:12.079 --> 00:34:13.876
That's not the way it happened.

00:34:18.118 --> 00:34:20.484
We'll see what your Captain
has to say about this.

00:34:20.521 --> 00:34:22.045
When I'm finished with you,

00:34:22.089 --> 00:34:24.114
you'll never wear
that uniform again.

00:34:24.158 --> 00:34:25.455
I can't let you do that.

00:34:25.492 --> 00:34:26.459
No, Tom, don't. Stop!

00:34:26.493 --> 00:34:27.482
No!

00:34:41.008 --> 00:34:43.067
The cycle's ended.

00:34:49.683 --> 00:34:52.345
No neural damage
that I can detect.

00:34:52.386 --> 00:34:55.753
Captain, I must consult
with Ensign Kim immediately.

00:34:55.789 --> 00:34:57.620
With Kim? Why?

00:34:57.658 --> 00:35:00.354
I assume he has access
to Professor Ren's research.

00:35:00.394 --> 00:35:02.919
I believe it will explain
not only why Lieutenant Paris

00:35:03.030 --> 00:35:05.658
has been accused of a murder
he did not commit,

00:35:05.699 --> 00:35:08.167
but also why the Numiri
chose to attack us.

00:35:14.307 --> 00:35:16.605
His condition has
continued to deteriorate.

00:35:16.643 --> 00:35:20.238
He'll have serious brain damage
if the implants are not removed.

00:35:20.280 --> 00:35:23.249
We are not a barbaric people,
Captain.

00:35:23.283 --> 00:35:25.717
This was meant as punishment
not torture.

00:35:25.752 --> 00:35:26.719
I see no alternative

00:35:26.753 --> 00:35:28.584
but to remove the implants,
do you?

00:35:28.622 --> 00:35:31.147
There is no legal precedent,
of course,

00:35:31.191 --> 00:35:33.523
but we can petition
the courts immediately.

00:35:33.560 --> 00:35:36.222
I cannot assure you'll find

00:35:36.263 --> 00:35:38.857
an alternative sentence
more to your liking.

00:35:38.899 --> 00:35:42.130
We're still committed to proving
his innocence, Minister.

00:35:42.169 --> 00:35:46.265
When do you intend
to return him to our custody?

00:35:46.306 --> 00:35:47.898
Due to the nature
of his condition,

00:35:47.941 --> 00:35:50.171
we're concerned
that our transporting device

00:35:50.210 --> 00:35:52.576
might cause
further medical complications.

00:35:52.612 --> 00:35:54.910
So we're sending him back
by shuttlecraft.

00:35:54.948 --> 00:35:57.416
They'll leave this ship
in one hour.

00:35:57.451 --> 00:36:00.477
I'll make the necessary
preparations.

00:36:14.534 --> 00:36:16.468
This is all your fault,
you know?

00:36:16.503 --> 00:36:17.765
My fault?

00:36:17.804 --> 00:36:20.602
Yeah, I consider you
the conscience I never had.

00:36:20.640 --> 00:36:23.609
You're supposed to keep me
on the straight and narrow.

00:36:23.643 --> 00:36:25.508
I tried to warn you.

00:36:25.545 --> 00:36:27.877
Funny, so did she.

00:36:27.914 --> 00:36:30.144
If it had been me,
I would have stayed

00:36:30.183 --> 00:36:32.117
as far away
from her as possible.

00:36:32.152 --> 00:36:35.417
Someday it will be you, Harry.

00:36:35.455 --> 00:36:37.753
You'll meet her,

00:36:37.791 --> 00:36:41.056
and you'll know it's wrong from
the first moment you see her.

00:36:41.094 --> 00:36:44.029
And you'll know there's nothing
you can do about it.

00:36:45.065 --> 00:36:46.327
Here they come.

00:36:46.366 --> 00:36:50.666
Numiri patrol approaching,
bearing 067 mark 24.

00:36:50.704 --> 00:36:51.966
Red Alert.

00:36:52.005 --> 00:36:53.370
On screen.

00:36:53.406 --> 00:36:56.603
Range, 100,000 kilometers
and closing.

00:36:56.643 --> 00:36:58.736
They're changing course,
Captain.

00:36:58.778 --> 00:37:00.746
They're going straight
for the shuttle

00:37:00.780 --> 00:37:03.271
just as you said
they would, Lieutenant.

00:37:04.317 --> 00:37:05.443
Shuttle to Voyager.

00:37:05.485 --> 00:37:07.350
They've locked
a tractor beam on us.

00:37:07.387 --> 00:37:08.752
Offer no resistance, Harry.

00:37:08.788 --> 00:37:09.755
Acknowledged.

00:37:09.789 --> 00:37:11.916
Hey, Tuvok.

00:37:11.958 --> 00:37:13.448
I know
it's a little late to ask,

00:37:13.493 --> 00:37:16.690
but you're sure you've got the
logic of this thing worked out?

00:37:16.730 --> 00:37:19.858
If I am incorrect,
we will know it shortly.

00:37:19.900 --> 00:37:22.528
Well, that makes me feel
a whole lot better.

00:37:24.137 --> 00:37:25.968
We're being boarded.

00:37:33.213 --> 00:37:34.805
He's the one.

00:37:43.823 --> 00:37:46.724
This is Captain Kathryn Janeway
of the Federation

00:37:46.760 --> 00:37:48.489
Starship Voyager.

00:37:48.528 --> 00:37:51.895
You have illegally seized
one of our shuttlecraft.

00:37:51.932 --> 00:37:54.526
I warned you that you were
entering a war zone

00:37:54.568 --> 00:37:56.229
at your own risk.

00:37:56.269 --> 00:37:57.395
Yes.

00:37:57.437 --> 00:37:59.098
We appreciated that warning

00:37:59.139 --> 00:38:01.130
and took
appropriate precautions.

00:38:01.174 --> 00:38:03.233
If you read the sensor readouts

00:38:03.276 --> 00:38:05.301
in front of you,
you will see that the shuttle

00:38:05.345 --> 00:38:08.781
is carrying 40 tons
of thalmerite explosives...

00:38:08.815 --> 00:38:11.249
enough to destroy your ship.

00:38:11.284 --> 00:38:15.914
I'm prepared to detonate
those explosives in 30 seconds

00:38:16.022 --> 00:38:18.820
if you do not release
our vessel.

00:38:18.858 --> 00:38:21.258
End transmission.

00:38:26.733 --> 00:38:28.291
The shuttle's being released.

00:38:28.335 --> 00:38:30.269
The Numiri ship is withdrawing.

00:38:30.303 --> 00:38:32.396
Tractor the shuttle
and take us into low orbit.

00:38:32.439 --> 00:38:34.805
Cancel Red Alert.

00:38:34.841 --> 00:38:38.140
Mr. Paris, how soon
before your next cycle?

00:38:38.178 --> 00:38:39.941
Seven hours.

00:38:39.980 --> 00:38:42.312
That should be enough time
to clear this up.

00:38:42.349 --> 00:38:46.251
Mr. Tuvok,
this is your show now.

00:38:46.286 --> 00:38:47.776
With your permission,

00:38:47.821 --> 00:38:49.516
I would like to invite
all interested parties

00:38:49.556 --> 00:38:51.956
to meet at the scene
of the murder in two hours.

00:38:52.025 --> 00:38:54.516
I'll invite the Minister myself.

00:39:00.066 --> 00:39:02.330
Lieutenant Paris was not
the man Professor Ren saw

00:39:02.369 --> 00:39:03.597
before he was murdered.

00:39:03.637 --> 00:39:05.332
Not the man...

00:39:05.372 --> 00:39:08.068
But it was clearly
established at the trial.

00:39:08.108 --> 00:39:09.075
It is true.

00:39:09.109 --> 00:39:10.406
Paris' image was seen

00:39:10.443 --> 00:39:12.411
in the memories
examined during the trial.

00:39:12.445 --> 00:39:13.571
However,

00:39:13.613 --> 00:39:15.513
that is because someone
altered the engrams

00:39:15.548 --> 00:39:17.345
from Professor Ren's brain.

00:39:17.384 --> 00:39:20.114
But that simply isn't possible
for this procedure.

00:39:20.153 --> 00:39:22.781
I would suggest, sir,
that there is no such thing

00:39:22.822 --> 00:39:25.791
as a technology that is
entirely safe from tampering.

00:39:25.825 --> 00:39:27.315
You're forgetting one thing.

00:39:27.360 --> 00:39:30.022
I was here and I saw him do it.

00:39:30.063 --> 00:39:31.428
On the contrary,

00:39:31.464 --> 00:39:33.728
I have not forgotten
your statement, Mrs. Ren.

00:39:33.767 --> 00:39:37.134
However, I now know
it is clearly false.

00:39:37.170 --> 00:39:40.936
Just what was in that tea
you gave me, Lidell?

00:39:40.974 --> 00:39:44.740
Is this just idle speculation,
or do you have some evidence?

00:39:44.778 --> 00:39:48.214
Mr. Paris, would you please
stand next to Mrs. Ren?

00:39:48.248 --> 00:39:49.476
What for?

00:39:49.516 --> 00:39:51.143
If you wouldn't mind.

00:39:56.356 --> 00:39:58.654
The man Professor Ren
observed with his wife

00:39:58.692 --> 00:40:01.786
was virtually equal
in height to her.

00:40:01.828 --> 00:40:04.661
Clearly, Lieutenant Paris
is several centimeters taller.

00:40:04.698 --> 00:40:07.667
How do you know
what my husband saw?

00:40:07.701 --> 00:40:08.895
Vulcans have the ability

00:40:08.935 --> 00:40:12.132
to meld telepathically
with another's mind.

00:40:12.172 --> 00:40:13.867
I observed
your husband's memories

00:40:13.907 --> 00:40:15.397
as Lieutenant Paris
went through his cycle.

00:40:15.442 --> 00:40:18.707
I watched as the killer
stabbed Professor Ren

00:40:18.745 --> 00:40:21.509
right here,
through the intercostal space

00:40:21.548 --> 00:40:23.948
between the eighth
and ninth right ribs...

00:40:23.983 --> 00:40:26.713
the exact location
of the Banean heart.

00:40:26.753 --> 00:40:29.984
The killer clearly knew
Banean anatomy.

00:40:30.023 --> 00:40:32.355
Lieutenant Paris did not.

00:40:32.392 --> 00:40:35.953
Are we supposed to take
your word for all of this?

00:40:35.995 --> 00:40:38.122
There is additional evidence.

00:40:38.164 --> 00:40:41.156
For example,
we can now say for certain

00:40:41.201 --> 00:40:44.170
that Professor Ren
was murdered by a Numiri agent.

00:40:44.204 --> 00:40:45.228
What?

00:40:45.271 --> 00:40:46.329
Lieutenant,

00:40:46.373 --> 00:40:48.671
did you notice the stream
of symbols and numbers

00:40:48.708 --> 00:40:50.266
that were superimposed
on the images?

00:40:50.310 --> 00:40:52.005
Symbols?

00:40:52.078 --> 00:40:54.478
Well, yeah, I guess I did.

00:40:54.514 --> 00:40:55.674
I didn't know what they meant.

00:40:55.715 --> 00:40:57.444
I thought they were
part of the procedure.

00:40:57.484 --> 00:40:59.281
In researching this procedure,

00:40:59.319 --> 00:41:01.651
I found no other reference
to this phenomenon.

00:41:01.688 --> 00:41:03.087
I have now confirmed

00:41:03.123 --> 00:41:05.591
that these symbols and numbers
were equations

00:41:05.625 --> 00:41:08.059
taken from Professor Ren's
weapons research.

00:41:08.094 --> 00:41:11.427
Someone intended them to be
delivered to the Numiri.

00:41:11.464 --> 00:41:13.329
You're saying somebody
used his brain

00:41:13.366 --> 00:41:15.664
to send secret data
to our enemy?

00:41:15.702 --> 00:41:17.260
He was a logical courier.

00:41:17.303 --> 00:41:19.771
The Numiri agents knew he could
leave the planet's surface

00:41:19.806 --> 00:41:21.330
without raising suspicion.

00:41:21.374 --> 00:41:24.901
The Numiri made two attempts
to gain access to Mr. Paris.

00:41:24.944 --> 00:41:27.606
They attacked just after
he returned to Voyager,

00:41:27.647 --> 00:41:29.615
and then again
when he was in the shuttle.

00:41:29.649 --> 00:41:32.209
Someone on the surface
had to be informing the Numiri

00:41:32.252 --> 00:41:33.913
of Lieutenant Paris' movements.

00:41:33.953 --> 00:41:35.887
Do you know who did this?

00:41:35.922 --> 00:41:39.380
You knew when Mr. Paris
would be in transit, Minister.

00:41:39.426 --> 00:41:41.417
But the doctor is the one

00:41:41.461 --> 00:41:43.986
who encouraged you
to release him to our custody.

00:41:44.030 --> 00:41:48.524
He is also the one who performed
the implant procedure.

00:41:48.568 --> 00:41:51.867
I know of no one else who had
the opportunity and knowledge

00:41:51.905 --> 00:41:53.236
to carry out this plan.

00:41:55.775 --> 00:41:58.767
I'm not going
to listen to any of this.

00:41:58.812 --> 00:42:01.940
I really would like you
to listen, Doctor.

00:42:02.015 --> 00:42:04.108
Would you please
stand again, Mrs. Ren.

00:42:07.487 --> 00:42:09.216
So we're the same height.

00:42:09.255 --> 00:42:10.882
It proves nothing.

00:42:10.924 --> 00:42:12.255
I never saw this woman

00:42:12.292 --> 00:42:14.157
prior to the death
of her husband.

00:42:14.194 --> 00:42:16.560
I was never even
in this house before today.

00:42:16.596 --> 00:42:19.121
You forget the other witness
who was here

00:42:19.165 --> 00:42:20.962
on the night of the murder,
Doctor.

00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:24.163
Would you mind
asking her to come in?

00:42:41.488 --> 00:42:45.390
It appears that you are
no stranger to Neeka, Doctor.

00:42:49.696 --> 00:42:51.857
He lied to me, Tom.

00:42:51.898 --> 00:42:54.332
No one was supposed
to get hurt.

00:42:54.367 --> 00:42:57.768
You know I could never
do anything to hurt you.

00:43:00.607 --> 00:43:02.404
Yeah.

00:43:02.442 --> 00:43:03.773
You could.

00:43:29.902 --> 00:43:31.665
Tuvok.

00:43:31.704 --> 00:43:33.399
Mr. Paris.

00:43:34.707 --> 00:43:37.505
There are some who'd say
you risked my future

00:43:37.543 --> 00:43:40.603
on the eyewitness
identification of a dog.

00:43:40.646 --> 00:43:42.876
It seemed a necessary step

00:43:42.915 --> 00:43:45.475
to ensure a truthful resolution.

00:43:45.518 --> 00:43:50.820
Well... I appreciate
you sticking up for me.

00:43:50.857 --> 00:43:52.950
I owe you one.

00:43:52.992 --> 00:43:56.257
I conducted
a criminal investigation.

00:43:56.295 --> 00:43:58.354
If you had been guilty,
I assure you

00:43:58.398 --> 00:44:01.026
I would have pursued the truth
just as vigilantly.

00:44:01.067 --> 00:44:03.433
You have no debt to me,
Mr. Paris.

00:44:07.974 --> 00:44:10.135
How come I always see you
down here

00:44:10.176 --> 00:44:11.803
eating alone, Lieutenant?

00:44:11.844 --> 00:44:15.803
I prefer to read
rather than engage in...

00:44:15.848 --> 00:44:18.874
What do humans call it...
short talk?

00:44:18.918 --> 00:44:20.317
Close enough.

00:44:22.221 --> 00:44:24.451
You don't make
many friends that way.

00:44:24.490 --> 00:44:26.424
Perhaps.

00:44:29.328 --> 00:44:32.957
Well, like it or not,

00:44:32.999 --> 00:44:35.433
you've made one today,
Mr. Tuvok.
